(3480633, 486930, 60614, '<td valign="top">Oh what I would give to be in my own kayak now.  This place looks lush and green.  The water almost looks bronze which compliments the green.  This would be a nice gift.</td>', 'Oh what I would give to be in my own kayak now.  This place looks lush and green.  The water almost looks bronze which compliments the green.  This would be a nice gift.', '2007-03-22 06:27:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3480640, 486645, 35602, '<td valign="top">Color balance seems to orangy.  Also, it looks like you tried focusing on the bottom of the lens, but the eyes are first drawn to the top OM-System tag, which is very soft.  I would adjust the focus to go where the eyes are drawn first, since it makes the entire image look oof.</td>', 'Color balance seems to orangy.  Also, it looks like you tried focusing on the bottom of the lens, but the eyes are first drawn to the top OM-System tag, which is very soft.  I would adjust the focus to go where the eyes are drawn first, since it makes the entire image look oof.', '2007-03-22 06:36:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(3480641, 485539, 35602, '<td valign="top">Could be better focus and background really makes the entire image kind of melt into itself, causing the eyes to really not see the snake all that well.</td>', 'Could be better focus and background really makes the entire image kind of melt into itself, causing the eyes to really not see the snake all that well.', '2007-03-22 06:38:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(3480647, 486922, 35602, '<td valign="top">Nice exposure on the snow capped mountains, but the foreground looks like the exposure was adjusted alot, which created a very flat, detailless area.  I wonder if you had exposed more for the foreground, then worked on the mountain if it would have worked better.  Even a nd filter for just the mountain would have equalized the light better.  Anyway, images such as this are really hard to get the right balance of light.</td>', 'Nice exposure on the snow capped mountains, but the foreground looks like the exposure was adjusted alot, which created a very flat, detailless area.  I wonder if you had exposed more for the foreground, then worked on the mountain if it would have worked better.  Even a nd filter for just the mountain would have equalized the light better.  Anyway, images such as this are really hard to get the right balance of light.', '2007-03-22 06:42:41.000000', NULL, 1),
